<Base title="Privacy — Sina Shiri" description="Privacy information for sina-shiri.com: no analytics, cookies or third-party scripts, GitHub Pages hosting and contact by email."><div class="wrap"><section class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span><h1>No analytics.<br />No cookies.</h1><p>This website is a set of static pages. It does not count visitors, set cookies or load third-party scripts.</p></section><article class="prose" style="padding-bottom:85px"><h2>No visit statistics or tracking</h2><p>The website contains no analytics, advertising or tracking code and does not use cookies or browser storage. Pages, fonts, images, videos and CV downloads are all served from sina-shiri.com itself, so no other website is contacted while you read.</p><h2>Hosting</h2><p>The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub’s documentation states that when a GitHub Pages site is visited, the visitor’s IP address is logged and stored for security purposes, whether or not the visitor is signed in to GitHub (<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" rel="noopener noreferrer">What is GitHub Pages? — Data collection</a>). These logs are kept by GitHub, not by Sina, and are covered by the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p><h2>Contacting Sina</h2><p>Contact works by email only. Email links on this website open your own mail app with Sina’s address filled in; topic links also add a subject line. Nothing is sent until you send it yourself. Your message travels from your email provider to Sina’s mailbox at sina-shiri.com and is handled there. The website does not receive, store or forward messages.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Links to GitHub, LinkedIn and other websites take you away from sina-shiri.com. Those sites have their own privacy practices. You do not need an account for anything on this website.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href={`mailto:${data.profile.email}`} data-cv-href="profile.email"><Text field="profile.email" /></a>.</p></article></div></Base>
